  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let G be a finite p-group and assume that all abelian normal subgroups of G\ncan be generated by k elements. Is it true that every abelian subgroup of G can be\ngenerated by 2k elements?\n   The k-th direct power of D16 shows that this bound would be best possible.\n                                                                                 L. Pyber",
